    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "# Frank3 E0-D2 data and pipeline validation"
      },
      {
        "id": "technical_summary",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Technical summary\n\n- **E0 passed:** Conda, the provided loader, two-GPU BF16/cuDNN/NCCL, local pi0_base, and W&B scalar logging all work. W&B logged zero artifacts.\n- **D0 is blocked:** only 22 of 25 PASS episodes have raw MCAP files, so a reproducible 25-episode conversion cannot start.\n- **D1 conditionally passed:** 10D current-EEF state, 7D anchor-relative Cartesian action, common-interval alignment, gripper mapping, and both rate profiles are frozen. No A/B or held-out val/test split is used.\n- **D2 passed:** causal time selection, endpoint identity, SO(3) encode/decode, and normalization round-trips passed on 824 complete horizons.\n\n**Decision: stop at D2.** Restore the three MCAP files, or explicitly approve a versioned 22of25 scope, before D3."
      },
      {
        "id": "scope_definitions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Scope and denominators\n\nRaw completeness uses the 25 PASS episodes in the manifest. Timestamp and schema results use the 22 currently readable episodes. D2 is a numerical spike on two named episodes; it performs no image conversion, no full LeRobot conversion, and no pi0 training.\n\nA valid full-horizon anchor has all 50 future camera intervals and passes every frozen source-age gate. Episode-tail padding is never treated as real action data."
      },
      {
        "id": "phase_status_block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "phase_table",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "raw_finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Three missing MCAP files are the only Critical completeness failure\n\nAcross the 22 readable episodes, topic counts match the manifest, images are consistently 480x640 RGB8, and EEF/gripper/qpos contain no non-finite values or schema drift. The three missing PASS entries have only visualization caches, which cannot reproduce the original observations and timestamps.",
        "sourceId": "d0_audit"
      },
      {
        "id": "coverage_block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "coverage_table",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "missing_block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "missing_table",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "alignment_finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## The frozen cam2 age gate retains 96.76% of nominal complete horizons\n\nThe common interval contains 8,815 cam1 anchors. Episode-tail constraints alone yield 7,715 complete horizons; applying the 100/50/10 ms cam2/EEF/gripper gates retains 7,465, a reduction of 250 (3.24%). All 18 invalid observations are caused by local cam2 staleness; EEF and gripper max ages are 33.70 ms and 3.92 ms.",
        "sourceId": "d0_audit"
      },
      {
        "id": "alignment_block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "alignment_table",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "d2_finding",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Both action-rate profiles pass every numerical gate\n\nThe 15 Hz profile uses t+1 through t+50. The 30 Hz profile uses midpoint then endpoint for each camera interval, producing 100 slots. Valid-anchor sets match, and every 30 Hz endpoint value and source timestamp is bit-exact with its 15 Hz counterpart.\n\nMaximum position/rotation/gripper round-trip errors are 0 m, 5.162e-8 rad, and 0. Maximum relative rotation is 0.981708 rad, safely below pi-0.1. Normalize then unnormalize has maximum error 1.110e-16.",
        "sourceId": "d2_spike"
      },
      {
        "id": "d2_block",
        "type": "table",
        "tableId": "d2_table",
        "layout": "full"
      },
      {
        "id": "methodology",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Frozen method and feature contract\n\n- Observation clock: cam1 MCAP log_time_ns with causal latest-not-after alignment.\n- State: 10D xyz + rotation6D + gripper; qpos remains audit-only.\n- Action: 7D base-frame delta xyz + body-frame SO(3) rotvec + target gripper, anchored at current measured EEF.\n- Targets: future measured EEF/gripper, explicitly a realized-waypoint proxy rather than an unrecorded desired command.\n- Statistics: min/max/mean/std/count/q01/q10/q50/q90/q99 on the effective 10D state and 7D action; 15 Hz and 30 Hz statistics remain separate.\n- Split: no A/B or held-out validation/test episodes; a future train-anchor subset may monitor in-distribution val loss only."
      },
      {
        "id": "limitations",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Limitations and robustness boundary\n\n1. D2 does not clear the D0 missing-data blocker and does not cover the unavailable episodes.\n2. current_pose is the measured configured EE frame in base, but the bag does not contain numerical F_T_EE/NE_T_EE. Real-robot deployment must reuse the same configured EE or apply an explicit fixed transform.\n3. There is no held-out evaluation. D2 proves numerical geometry and alignment behavior, not task success or generalization.\n4. Version 1 records chase-frame/irregular timing evidence but does not rewrite real time; stale cam2 observations are excluded only through the explicit age gate."
      },
      {
        "id": "next_steps",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Recommended next steps\n\n1. Prefer restoring the three missing MCAP files, then rerun D0 to reach 25/25.\n2. If restoration is impossible and rapid verification is acceptable, explicitly approve a new 22of25 derived manifest and dataset version.\n3. After D3 is unblocked, convert both profiles and compute their full statistics; train first on obs15/action15 only after D4, S0, and S1 pass.\n4. Confirm that collection and deployment use the same configured EE/TCP before a real-robot rollout."
      },
      {
        "id": "further_questions",
        "type": "markdown",
        "body": "## Decision required\n\nShould the project restore the three raw MCAP files and retain the 25-episode scope, or should it create an explicitly approved, versioned 22of25 rapid-verification scope?"
      }
    ]
  },
